[Event "vs 1.c4: White fianchettoes"]
[Opening "Other first moves"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. c4 e6 2. g3 d5 {Take the center.} 3. Bg2 Nf6 4. Nf3 Be7 5. O-O O-O {Castle. Simple and safe.} 6. b3 c5 {Take more space.} 7. Bb2 Nc6 *

[Event "vs 1.Nf3: King's Indian Attack"]
[Opening "Other first moves"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. Nf3 d5 {Take the center.} 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O Be7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 {Space on the queen side – that is where you play.} 7. e4 Nc6 8. Re1 b5 {Go forward on the queen side!} *

[Event "vs 1.Nf3: 2.c4"]
[Opening "Other first moves"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. Nf3 d5 2. c4 e6 {Hold d5 with a pawn.} 3. g3 Nf6 4. Bg2 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. d4 dxc4 {Take the pawn now – White has to spend time getting it back.} 7. Qc2 a6 8. Qxc4 b5 {Kick the queen.} 9. Qc2 Bb7 *

[Event "vs 1.f4: Bird's Opening"]
[Opening "Other first moves"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. f4 {Bird's Opening.} d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 g6 {Your bishop on g7 looks at the long diagonal.} 4. Be2 Bg7 5. O-O O-O 6. d3 c5 {Take space. Equal game.} *

[Event "vs 1.b3: Nimzo-Larsen"]
[Opening "Other first moves"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. b3 {The bishop will go to b2 and look at e5.} e5 {Take the center anyway.} 2. Bb2 Nc6 {Protect e5.} 3. e3 d5 4. Bb5 Bd6 {Protect e5 again and develop.} 5. f4 Qh4+ {A useful check!} 6. g3 Qe7 7. Nf3 f6 {e5 is rock solid.} *

